  "processFilter": {
    "question": "Whether a session's process filter holds for COM-Perf: FX-COM-001's exchange, its two processes the filter's, beside a decoy pair running the same exchange outside it, every process waiting to initialize COM until the filter was in place.",
    "answer": "It holds. In two runs, 64 calls paced and 256 unpaced, the session delivered the filtered pair's every call at both ends and not one record of the decoy pair - which made as many calls - or of any other process; nothing was lost. COM-Perf is raised in the process that makes or serves a call, so a capture scoped to named processes collects their calls alone.",
